{%- comment -%}
  Outputs the lowercase two-letter country the storefront is styled for.

  Markets with their own subfolder (czech, france, ireland, portugal, spain, sweden) keep the
  visitor's real country. Every root-domain market (poland, de, greece, hungary, romania,
  slovakia, slovenia, and every visitor Shopify drops into the DE fallback) gets 'pl', so the
  page looks exactly like Poland. Looks only: prices, catalog and checkout still follow the real market.

  Usage:
    {%- capture sf_country -%}{% render 'storefront-country' %}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign sf_country = sf_country | strip -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign own_country_markets = 'czech,france,ireland,portugal,spain,sweden' | split: ','
  if own_country_markets contains localization.market.handle
    echo localization.country.iso_code | downcase
  else
    echo 'pl'
  endif
-%}
